window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>*Please read the entire description before purchase. Content warnings below.*</p> <p>This audiobook is part two and not intended to be a standalone. It is recommended to listen to <i>Savior: Book One</i> prior to <i>Savior: Book Two.</i></p> <p>Now that her nightmare is over, Vanna and I are free to live our happily ever after like I promised her we would. Even if I have to kill for it. Those were my words to her. Words I intend to live up to. Though, as we have come to learn, the past rarely stays buried. Not even when it's left to rot in the Sonoran Desert.</p> <p>This time, it's my past that's come back to threaten our future together.</p> <p>I've found the happiness that has always evaded me in Vanna. She's my little piece of heaven I'd sell my soul to keep, and I'll be damned if demons from my past are going to take her from me.</p> <p>NOTE: Trauma can cause your brain to remain in a state of hyper-vigilance. It can cause you to suppress memory and impulse controls, trapping you in a constant state of intense emotional reactivity. The <i>Savior</i> audiobooks deal heavily with two main characters navigating life and relationships through and after trauma.</p> <p>As I write my characters true to who they are, they will be far from perfect, and might not make the same decisions you would. We all deal with things in our own ways. This is their story.</p> <p><i>Please mind the content warnings:</i> </p> <p>Contains explicit content: s3x, vi0lence, profanity, blasphemy, drama, pregnancy (complications, not described in graphic detail, mostly medical terminology), murder, self-harm, dismemberment, knife and gun violence, brief mention of child @ buse and human tr@ ffic king (@ buse not described)</p> <p>(These content warnings may make this audiobook seem darker than it actually is. \"Darkness\" is subjective. I’m just trying to cover all the bases.)<br> <br> Not intended for anyone under the age of 18.</p>"; 
